On Mon, 3 Apr 2006, Gary Olson wrote:
>
> Having just run into a statue of one of my former (unlucky) characters 
> (again), I pose this question:
> Where and how are statues saved? Are they saved in a file which can be 
> traded on hearse much like bones files are? If not, how difficult a code 
> change would be required to implement statue swapping?

Player statues come from one of two places, AFAICT:

   Sometimes a statue will be randomly created with a player's name, in 
which case the name, class, and race come out of the high-score table.

   If a bones level is created when a character dies by petrification,
then that bones level will contain a statue of the deceased, instead of
a grave. That statue is saved as an actual named item in a particular
place on the bones level, and can be traded along with the rest of the
bones level.

